      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:3:3:46:3",
      "text": [
        " قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ ( صلى الله عليه وآله ) خَيْرُ الصُّفُوفِ فِي الصَّلَاةِ الْمُقَدَّمُ وَ خَيْرُ الصُّفُوفِ فِي الْجَنَائِزِ الْمُؤَخَّرُ قِيلَ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ وَ لِمَ قَالَ صَارَ سُتْرَةً لِلنِّسَاءِ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from his father, from Al Nowfaly, from Al Sakuny, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘Rasool-Allah<sup>saww</sup> said: ‘The best of the rows regarding the (Prescribed) <span class=\"iTxt\">Salaat</span> is the first one, and the best of the rows regarding the funeral is the last one’. It was said, ‘O Rasool-Allah<sup>saww</sup>! And why is it so?’ He<sup>saww</sup> said: ‘For it to become a veil for the women’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "3. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from his father from al-Nawfaliy from al-Sakuniy who has said the following: “Abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, that the Messenger of Allah has said, ‘The best row in Salah (prayer) is the first row but the best row in Salah (prayer) for dead bodies is the last one.’ It was asked, ‘Why is it so, O Messenger of Allah?’ He (the Messenger of Allah) said, ‘It is a curtain for women.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
